 # Current state
 
+## Call and token efficiency evaluation
+
+The isolated `ark-call-efficiency` tree contains scoped Codex host-tool isolation, a measured
+default-instruction experiment and honest managed-session benchmark coverage. Baseline:
+30/30 checked attempts, 104 calls and 2,012,191 tokens on `codex:gpt-5.6-terra@medium`.
+Isolation-only: 30/30, 102 calls and 1,526,988 tokens. The first prompt candidate is rejected
+after one approval task stopped at a text-only permission request (29/30 overall). A scoped
+approval mapping correction passes a fresh 30/30 with 87 calls and 1,290,472 tokens. All
+18 focused safety and prompt-capture checks and workspace tests pass. The exact-source
+`scripts/ci.sh` gate passes. Real writing-app dogfood passes on the same named Codex model
+with unforced effort (4 and 3 words, total 7, manuscript unchanged). Explicit-effort writer
+startup failed twice before a model call: the optional usage-limit query and model listing
+exceeded the existing catalog deadline. That separate reliability fix is `d1bb1e0c`; the
+unforced-effort check does not establish explicit-effort startup reliability. Integration
+of this uncommitted tree is `06ad26dd`. All own build output has been cleaned.
+Vendor configuration changed outside the evaluation. Model, effort, fixtures and ARK budgets
+are fixed, but observed cross-condition differences are not strict causal savings. No commit
+or release occurred. Protocol, hashes, all failures and limitations:
+`bench/efficiency-2026-10-15/README.md`. Board: `958effaa`.
+
 ## Advanced artifact surfaces in development
 
 `ark-advanced-artifacts` implements ADR 0071: map/model classification, route-bound immutable
